✅ Time Series Regression: Training and Test should be in sequence (series)

✅ ML Regression: Training and Test can be random

=======================================


| Feature                 | Time Series Regression                    | Machine Learning Regression               |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| **Data Type**           | Time-dependent data                       | General tabular data                      |
| **Order of Data**       | Sequence matters                          | Sequence usually does not matter          |
| **Main Goal**           | Forecast future values                    | Predict target variable                   |
| **Example**             | Stock price prediction, sales forecasting | House price prediction, salary prediction |
| **Uses Past Values?**   | Yes (lag values, trends, seasonality)     | Not necessarily                           |
| **Patterns Considered** | Trend, Seasonality, Cyclic patterns       | Relationships between features and target |
| **Common Algorithms**   | ARIMA, SARIMA, Prophet, LSTM              | Linear Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost |
| **Input Example**       | Date + Previous Sales                     | Area, Bedrooms, Location                  |
| **Output Example**      | Next month's sales                        | House price                               |


============

Time Series Regression predicts future values using historical data arranged in time order and considers trend and seasonality.

Machine Learning Regression predicts a continuous target variable using independent features without necessarily considering time order.

============
