=================
from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression

model = LinearRegression()

model.fit(X_train, y_train)

prediction = model.predict(X_test)

===================
Purpose:

Learns relationship between features and target.
Predicts continuous values

====================

Time Series Regression

Description:
Time Series Regression is a forecasting technique used to predict future values based on historical data arranged in chronological order (time sequence). It analyzes patterns such as trend, seasonality, and past observations to make predictions.

Examples:

Stock Price Forecasting
Sales Forecasting
Weather Prediction
Demand Forecasting

Key Point: Time order is important.

==============

Machine Learning Regression

Description:
Machine Learning Regression is a supervised learning technique used to predict a continuous 
numerical value by learning the relationship between input features and a target variable. The order of data is generally not important.

Examples:

House Price Prediction
Salary Prediction
Insurance Cost Prediction
Student Score Prediction

Key Point: Relationship between features and target is important, not time order.

Simple Difference

Time Series Regression: Predicts future values using past time-based data.

Machine Learning Regression: Predicts a numerical value using input features regardless of time sequence.
